"title":"Domain separation and Decision Builder","description":"This is an overview of domain separation as it pertains to Decision Builder. Domain separation allows you to separate data, processes, and administrative tasks into logical groupings called domains. You can then control several aspects of this separation, including which users can see and access data.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/build-workflows/workflow-studio/domain-separation-decision-builder.html","release":"australia","product":"Workflow Studio","classification":"workflow-studio","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":1,"breadcrumb":["Decision tables reference","Decision tables","Workflow Studio","Build workflows"],"tags":["#build-workflows","#workflow-studio","#visual","#process-design","#flow-designer","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/build-workflows/workflow-studio/domain-separation-decision-builder.md"},
